    {
      "id": 119622,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-10-20T15:03:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The line of Sight rules for Tactics are very simple, so there are situations where they will fail a reality check.</p><p>Two targets have line of sight is there are no hexes between them that are higher than either of them.</p><p>So line of sight from an elevation 3 hex to an elevation 1 hex will be broken if it goes through any hex that is higher than elevation 1.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>By the rules if the Drone was farther away and every new hex between them was elevation 1, the elevation 2 hexes right next to bunker still block line of sight.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That doesn't stop you from house ruling the line of sight rules to be more realistic and complex, they just chose to keep line of sight rules incredibly simple for this game, and completely math free.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:52:53.054Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
